    "thesis": "Rubrik scores 55, a Hold with medium confidence, because strong and weak factors roughly cancel out. Revenue grew 37.89% year on year in the latest quarter and 42.45% on a trailing basis (growth score 84). The balance sheet is net cash with cash at 1.54 times debt (score 96), and the shares sit 54.74% above their 200-day average (trend score 90). Against that, quality scores only 28: operating margin is -18.31%, stock-based pay is 22.16% of revenue, and FCF margin is -2.62% once $344.3M of customer prepayments is stripped out, versus a reported 19.7%. Valuation scores 3, with price-to-sales at 15.222 and an FCF yield 5.382 points below the 10-year Treasury yield.",
